FINAL: Claude Shannon was born on April 30, 1916, and passed away on February 24, 2001. His three key contributions to information theory include: 1) The introduction of entropy as a measure of information content, 2) The development of the Nyquist–Shannon sampling theorem, and 3) The establishment of fundamental limits on data compression and transmission rates.
